  "id": "Compound::DB06738 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Ketobemidone exhibits a strong binding interaction with Cyp2c9, which is involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. This binding is consistent across multiple paths, suggesting a potential role in the enzymatic activity of Cyp2c19. The shared participation of Cyp2c9 in the epoxygenation and monooxygenation of arachidonic acid indicates that Ketobemidone may influence the activity of Cyp2c19 through a common metabolic pathway. The evidence suggests that Ketobemidone could modulate Cyp2c19's function by interacting with Cyp2c9, which in turn affects the metabolic processing of arachidonic acid. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Ketobemidone may impact Cyp2c19, although the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The observed scores and pathway connections support a mechanistic link between Ketobemidone and Cyp2c19, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise role of this interaction.",
